rent shows tends to skew  towards one of the Lesser episodes since  they are tasked with having to do a lot  of setup and Exposition but The Heirs of  the Dragon doesn't do this only in the  opening scene do we get Exposition and  to be fair it's kind of necessary to  establish where we are in the history of  Westeros after this though the writers  essentially plant us right into an  already existing world and do very  little Exposition they seamlessly blend  us into this narrative and allow the  audience to learn who the characters are  by seeing them react to different forms  of conflict no expository dialogue is  needed when each character is being  molded by different obstacles that tests  them like right away viserys is tested  by the birth complications of his new  child and then having to deal with  succession issues after the death of his  wife Damon trying to find some form of  purpose and dealing with the reality of  not being air anymore Bernier navigating  through all those obstacles while taking  on the responsibility of becoming the  new Heir and different Side characters  briefly cutting in in each scene to try  and sway each character's Minds with  their own wants and Wishes the show  quickly establishes and fully develops  each of its main characters as we are  thrown into an engaging story with  outstanding conflict like the birth  scene was so horrific and tragic that it  really sets the tone for the story to  come not to mention that a lot of the  dialogue scenes were all very  interesting especially when the topic of  succession comes up and we see viserys  break down and everyone trying to  influence him with their own benefits  then there's also a fun tournament with  jousting to add some spectacle into the  episode so overall this opening episode  is well balanced and acts as a perfect  introduction to House of the Dragon  Number 5 episode 2 the Rogue Prince this  may be an unpopular opinion but I like  the Rook Prince a little more than the  first episode this episode opens  immediately with a haunting feeling as  we first see what the crab feeder is  doing this both gives us some great  imagery on top of it giving what  cordless has to say some weights because  before this we didn't really know what  was happening in the stepstones so  quickly and efficiently this opening  makes us excited for this upcoming  conflict this then leads into a small  council meeting and in this scene we see  where nearer finally speak out which  essentially teases her independent  attitude and that leader quality is  starting to break through not only does  she have these triumphant character  moments but we also break renira down in  two separate scenes where she deals with  the loss of her mother and viserys  having to move on and find a new wife  each of these scenes hits a beautiful  emotional depth that absorbs the  audience with Millie's entrancing  performance this is to me what sold the  actors so well these small character  moments where they simply talk to one  another and go through a vast array of  emotions drips with so much Intrigue  these scenes are also imbued with a  great point of conflict in which if a  Series has to deal with having to find a  new wife this Dynamic has a lot of depth  because every character has a stake in  it and can add something new like  everyone having their own mischievous  motivations and seeing viscers go along  with some of them like talking with  Elena was funny then this isn't even  mentioning the best part which is the  10th showed on a Dragonstone between the  Otto and Daemon the amount of tension  within this scene was so powerful from  the music slowly building up the fog  obstructing the Sun and creating a tense  atmosphere how unpredictable Damon is  and karaxi is showing up made this seem  so fun to watch then it takes an  unpredictable turn where Nero shows up  to solve the confrontation without any  Bloodshed thus acting as her big moments  and this moment also unlocks her theme  that she essentially earns Here  andronera's theme is probably my  favorite throughout the entire show the  Rogue Prince is pretty great through and  through and even the cinematography is  at its best in my opinion  number four episode three second of his  name initially I wasn't a huge fan of  the first half of the episode but I've  come to really like the journeys that  both were near and viserys go on the  parallels to how they both treat their  anguishes were interesting since we're  nearer chooses to run away and be  rebellious while viserys chooses to  drown himself in wine seeing him grapple  with the annoyance of politicking and  wondering if he made the right decision  to make her near his Heir allows us to  see if it serves without any barriers  kings are always really reserved but  here he's pouring out so many emotions  that we are allowed to witness and feast  on like the bonfire in particular was  the peak of the episode in my opinion  because of this then rhaenyra also boils  over to a degree and lets out all of her  anger while killing the boar she's so  overcome with the responsibilities of  growing up having to marry and being a  pawn for her father in terms of politics  that it's driving her crazy so her  showing back up to the camp drenched in  blood makes her seem like a badass and  Commander respect I also like the small  details for how and being kind of turned  on by that kind of foreshadowing the  future this dual Journey has some great  character development and even the  resolution afterward and King's Landing  was pretty touching the series deciding  to let Rainier choose who to marry was a  great compromise but yet again that's  not necessarily a good choice to make as  a king then we have the stepstones  conflict to me the best aspect of this  battle is easily Damon Targaryen this  was a great showcase for the man where  he risks everything to prove himself and  even turns down help from his brother  the rush he makes was some intense  action and I hope people have moved away  from the Aero controversy because relax  the man still gets hit like three times  my only issue with this portion of the  episode is the fact that it doesn't  really last that long the actual battle  only lasts like 2 minutes and then it  quickly ends when Damon walks out with a  crab feeder's corpse it gives off a bit  of an anticlimactic feeling and if they  had more impressive slash longer takes  of action following Our Heroes then this  episode would maybe crack my top three  for the season but it's still pretty  good and acts as a fun final sequence to  an already great episode  number three episode 10 The Black Queen  some people may feel compelled to put  this episode at number one because of  the insane final scene with vegar but I  think this finale has a bit too much  setup and that's in regards to wartime  preparations it's nice to see but it's  not something that you would expect  within a finale that's normally packed  with a lot of payoff which the payoff we  do get is amazing we're Nera having a  miscarriage was extremely uncomfortable  and drastically increased attention at  the beginning of the episode reniro  becoming Queen was immensely uplifted by  Ramin jawadi's wonderful score Corliss  finally allying himself with renera was  so satisfying when his theme played and  the death of luceris was batshit  insanity and had some of the best action  intention build up we've ever seen if  the episode was just these scenes with  maybe one setup scene cut out or even  just the ending 10-minute sequence on  repeats then it would have been hard to  not put this episode at number one but  since there's a lot of Roundtable  discussions within this episode it's it  slows down that fast and Fun Pace  cutting out one of the setup scenes  could be better to keep the pace moving  more quickly but it's hard to say that  since they are needed and are still good  this is obviously a minor issue and  these are things I need to address when  the top three episodes are so close in  quality I can honestly argue why this  episode in the next two could be number  one and at the end of the day it will  come down to opinion one thing that we  can all agree on though is how perfect  the ending of the season is aim and  chasing luceris on vegar was so intense  given the size difference and the  setting of the scene hiding away this  massive threat in the Thundering clouds  was terrifying and the action was  perfectly presented by not hiding the  VFX in terrible lighting conditions the  fact that we can follow the action with  ease is refreshing and it never breaks  our immersion 10 minutes of pure  adrenaline and this scene alone carries  the episode  number two episode seven driftmark when  this episode released it was my favorite  and it almost retained that spot the  reason it was there in the first place  is that this episode has a perfect  collection of scenes nothing feels out  of place there's no downbeat and it just  keeps getting better the episode opened  strong with an ensemble of characters  interacting with each other I tend to  love these scenes because of how much  depth is here and the number of small  interactions that happens between every  character everyone has a moment to shine  here and the writers officially set up  certain dynamics that will be an  integral later on then we have an  engrossing debate between rhaenys and  Corliss their motivation is perfectly  contrast with each other which allows  for some great dialogue two lines in the  scene are even quoted in the trailer and  then we have renir and Damon on the  beach now I like the writing of this  scene it's just that due to the dark  lighting we can't really see their  reactions that well kind of feels like a  hindrance in an otherwise integral scene  between these two characters who are  getting emotional but that's the only  small flaw within this episode this  leads into Eamon taming vegar and this  was a great display of awe-inspiring  scale the action as Eamon tries to  desperately hold on was so gripping this  is followed by aemond having a violent  confrontation with her near his children  which I honestly did not know how that  scene was going to play out so an aemond  loses an eye I was genuinely surprised  this sets up the best scene of the  episode in which Allison demands Justice  for that so many aspects about the scene  are amazing we have viserys desperately  trying to keep everyone at Bay the  awkward silence as everyone acknowledges  the truth about our nearest children the  harsh back and forth dialogue and the  explosive ending as Allison vs raniero  with viserys's dagger truly a great  Climax and somehow the episode doesn't  end here it ends with a crazy Encore of  laner's fake out death which even that  scene has some impressive writing in  that the writers lead you to believe  that laner actually dies but doesn't and  gets a happy ending this episode is flat  out stacked and has great character work  action plot twists love and even Auto  Hightower gets reinstated as a hand  easily top two worthy and is really  close to being in my top spot but the  next episode has something very special  about it number one episode 8 the lord  of the tides yeah you know why this  episode is at number one the Last Supper  is easily the best scene in the season  and is a pure Rush of happiness every  time I watch it I don't know how many  people here watch Rick and Morty but I'm  like the Rick who's held prisoners they  make him watch the same Happy scene over  and over to farm serotonin but for me  that scene on replay is visera smiling  it's such a purely wholesome moment that  I couldn't help but shed a tear when  first watching it throughout the entire  season we come to love visceros and the  tragedy of his entire bodily Decay mixes  feel so bad for him so seeing this last  moment in which he gets to witness his  family be happy one more time his  extreme really precious and is not  something I was expecting to come out of  this dark show that and the rest of this  scene is so great in which he Reveals  His Face to everyone and gives a  heartwarming speech along with renera  trying to reconcile with Allison so this  is the perfect example of the Calm  before the storm then for the rest of  the episode there's really no down  moments Ranier and Damon visit viserys  while the man is in agony Allison having  to deal with a handmaid getting raped by  aegon which in particular was a great  showcase for the handmade actor in terms  of acting Alison roasting aegon him  being a douche renera awkwardly meeting  up with the rhaenys after killing her  son viserys's makeup routine and some  other quick scenes that are equally  intriguing however this wouldn't be my  number one spot without another standout  scene which is the throne room debate  for the succession of driftmark  throughout this entire scene you know  this hearing is rigged in vaman's favor  so you have no idea how her Nero will  come out of the situation on top and I  assumed she wouldn't so to have busy tea  show up like an absolute Legend works as  an excellent twist and is also severely  uplifted by Ramin jawadi going ham on  the score and I also love the fact that  the director draws this moment out so  much by having the Stars slowly walk  across the entire Throne Room really  emphasizing how much of an impressive  feat this is then vaman explodes and  Damon removes his head so overall great  escalation in terms of plot points and  twists within the scene and it just  keeps getting better as you go through  it with this shocking death Triumph a  moment from viserys one of the most  heartwarming moments in Game of Thrones  history and a collection of solid scenes  in between those bangers mix this a  goaded episode of House of the Dragon  thank you for watching and let me know  in the comments what your ranking would  be  [Music]  foreign
 

